{
  "title": "Morel-Lavallee Lesion",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/trauma/422820/morel-lavallee-lesion",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Aug 26 2026",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "A Morel-Lavallee Lesion (MLL) is a closed traumatic soft tissue degloving injury characterized by separation of the dermis from the underlying fascia due to a shearing force.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis requires high a index of suspicion with presence of an area of ecchymosis, swelling, fluctuance and skin hypermobility in the polytrauma patient with underlying fractures.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is generally operative irrigation and debridement for most lesions given the proximity to planned surgical incisions and increased risk of infection.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "present in up to 8% of acetabulum fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "most often along proximal lateral thigh, in the **peritrochanteric region**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "to a lesser extent gluteal, lumbosacral, and abdominal areas",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "due to hypermobility of skin in these regions",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Risk factors",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**high-energy, shearing trauma**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "divided into 4 stages:",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "shearing forces to soft-tissue envelope lead to separation of the dermis from the underlying fascia",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "injured lymphatics and vasculature from the injured subdermal plexus produce",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/422820/images/morel_lavalee_2c.jpg",
                      "caption": "Fluid in Morel lesion"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "these components are then replaced by serosanguinous fluid as the lesion enlarges",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "finally, if left untreated during the acute stage, local inflammation leads to pseudocapsule formation and lesion maturation as the body attempts to sequester the space",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "bacterial colonization of the fluid occurs in up to 46% of lesions",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "orthopaedic conditions",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**pelvic and acetabular fractures**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**proximal femur fractures**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Anatomy of soft tissues (order of layers from superifical to deep)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "epidermis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "dermis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "subcutaneous fat",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/422820/images/morel-lavallee-anatomy-illustration.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "MLL develops deep to subctuaneous fat and superfical to deep fascia",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "deep fascia",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "muscle",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "History",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "there should be high clinical suspician for a MLL in a polytrauma patient with a high-energy mechanism",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "often minimally symptomatic or marginalized due to underlying distracting injuries or patient body habitus",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "up to **33% of lesions are missed** at the time of index evaluation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "chronic lesions may lead to cosmetic issues",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "inspection",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/422820/images/morel_lavalee_2a.jpg",
                  "caption": "Morel Lavalle Lesion"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "ecchymosis, swelling, fluctuance and skin hypermobility",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/422820/images/morel_lavalee_1a.jpg",
                      "caption": "Morel Lavalee Lesion"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**skin discoloration** may not be apparent until several days later",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "neurovascular",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "key indicator is paresthesias of overlying skin",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "evaluate underlying proximal femur, acetabulum or pelvis fractures",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "may show soft tissue swelling",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "CT",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/422820/images/left_thigh_mll_-soft_tissue_window..jpg",
              "caption": ""
            },
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/422820/images/left_thigh_morel_lavalle_-_bone_window..jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "CT of the area of interest often obtained due to high-energy nature of the injury, underlying fracture, or abdominal/pelvic injury",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "used to measure size of lesion to determine management",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "soft tissue windows will show slice of fluid within fascial plane",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Ultrasound",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "can be used to localize lesion for percutaneous treatment",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "hypoechoic space superficial to fascial layer",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "generally not required for diagnosis but will best demonstrate extent of the lesion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "average size reported to be 30 x 12 cm",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "fluid-filled space is often identifiable on T1- and T2-weighted MRI sequences.",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "acute lesions are hypointense on T1-weighted images and hyperintense on T2-weighted sequences",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "subacute lesions are homogenously hyperintense on T1- and T2-weighted sequences, with a peripheral capsule that is hypointense on both T1- and T2-weighted sequences",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "compressive therapy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "small lesions (< than 50 cm3)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "resolutional of smaller lesions can be successful with compressive therapy but this requries high patient compliance",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "percutaneous drainage with drain placement",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "small lesions (< than 50 cm3)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "considered inferior to open debridement given inability to perform an adequate debridement of necrotic tissue",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Single-incision irrigation and debridement (I&D)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "relative indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "large lesions (> 50 cm3) or persistent MLL having failed non-operative management",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "lesion is not in the way of surgical approach for fracture",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "successful resolution of lesion in up to 75% of cases with single I&D",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "more than I&D may be required for very large lesions",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Dual-incision I&D",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "relative indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "lesion overlies surgical approach for fracture management",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "MLL discovered intra-operatively during surgical approach",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "lesions near a surgical approach have a higher rate of infection and may require serial I&Ds prior to definitive managment of underlying fracture",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Open debridement with resection of the fibrous capsule",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "relative indication",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "chronic MLLs with pseudocyst formation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "mixed, often requires multiple surgeries for eradication",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Techniques",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Compressive therapy**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "most common modalities are ace wraps, compression bandages, bike shorts (for proximal thigh lesions)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Percutaneous drainage with drain placement**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "use ultrasound to localize lesion then make 1-2 cm incision overlying leison",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "insert a suction tip into the lesion to remove hemorrhagic fluid",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "irrigate with normal saline",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Single incision I&D**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "incision centered over MLL",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "aggressive debridement of cavity performed with scrub brush, Cobb and/or other instruments",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "placement of a drain exiting away from lesion (consider using 15 Fr or larger drain)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "recommend leaving drain until minimal output (< 20-30 cc/day)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "primary closure of lesion versus delayed closure",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "controversial",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "depends on size of lesion",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "delayed closure would involve wound vaccum placement and repeat I&D and closure in 48-72 hours",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Dual-incision I&D**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "incision over most proximal aspect of lesion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "counter incision over most distal aspect of lesion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "similar to single incision for rest of treatment EXCEPT",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "primary closure of most proximal incision during first I&D",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "delayed closure of distal incision with wound vacuum (VAC)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "return in 48-72 hours for repeat I&D through distal incision and closure",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
